    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0624" n="614" xml:id="pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/1–1449</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-01-14">January 14, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Record</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Mr. Lovett called on his return at noon from the Cabinet meeting and requested
                    that I record in writing the following:</p>
                <p>In accordance with the Department’s suggestion, the subject matter of the
                    attached memorandum<anchor n="45" xml:id="d599-f1"/> was discussed at a full
                    Cabinet meeting today at which the Vice President-elect<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d599-f2"/> and Mr. Hoffman were present. Mr. Hoffman advocated his
                    point of view for three-quarters of an hour, using the same arguments he had
                    employed on January 7 in Mr. Lovett’s office with Messrs. Labouisse,
                    Butterworth, Cleveland and Bruce also being present. Mr. Lovett mentioned some
                    of the larger implications involved in the problem and read the two pertinent
                    excerpts from Title IV of the ECA Act.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d599-f3"/> The
                    President polled the whole Cabinet who unanimously voted that the memorandum
                    represented their considered attitude.</p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary also left with the President the attached memorandum
                    regarding rehabilitation projects in Formosa<anchor n="48" xml:id="d599-f4"/>
                    and gave a copy to Mr. Hoffman.</p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary also gave to the President the memorandum regarding the
                    situation in Tsingtao and Formosa, a copy of which is also attached.<anchor
                        n="49" xml:id="d599-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butterworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d599-a1.xml" xpointer="d599-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
